# Bootstrapping Stage 1 Review Checklist (v4 section 5, Step 5)

This checklist is based on Phase 2/3 automated detection results. Each representative sample requires manual review. Per v4: *"Minimum 2 samples per cluster manually reviewed. Split or exclude cluster on problems."*

Mark each item: `[X]` (vulnerable), `[N]` (not vulnerable), `[partial]` (conditional).

---

## C1. Endpoint-level Auth/Authz Gaps

**Candidate scale**: N endpoints / N modules (detail: `c1/auth_enumeration.md`)

### Representative Samples (v4 Step 4 priority: risk > unclear sanitizer > path complexity)

#### C1-s1 (highest risk) — {{Description}}
- [ ] **`{{Module}}/{{Path}}/{{Controller}}.java`** — `{{HTTP_METHOD}} {{endpoint}}`
  - Checks:
    - [ ] Controller-level auth annotation (`@PreAuthorize`, `@Secured`) present?
    - [ ] WebConfig `addInterceptors()` has Auth/Login interceptor?
    - [ ] Service-layer signature/HMAC/token verification present?
    - [ ] Gateway enforcement evidence (operational, not code)?
  - Verdict:
    - [ ] Vulnerable (code-level controls: 0)
    - [ ] Not vulnerable
    - [ ] Partial — operational evidence pending

#### C1-s2 (largest scale) — {{Description}}
- [ ] **`{{Module}}/{{Path}}/{{Controller}}.java`** — N endpoints
  - Checks: (same as C1-s1)
  - **Confusion prevention note**: `AuthenticationService`/`authNo` names may exist but serve a different purpose (e.g., recipient verification, not API caller auth). Always verify auth layer (caller vs recipient vs session).
  - Verdict:
    - [ ] Vulnerable
    - [ ] Not vulnerable
    - [ ] Partial

