## C2. Hardcoded Shared-Secret

**Candidate scale**: N endpoints / N modules

#### C2-s1 — {{Description}}
- [ ] **`{{Path}}`** — `{{endpoint}}`
  - Checks:
    - [ ] Shared secret in source code (constant field)?
    - [ ] Same secret across environments (dev/staging/prod)?
    - [ ] Failure path allows bypass (returns true on mismatch)?
  - Verdict:
    - [ ] Vulnerable
    - [ ] Not vulnerable

---

## C3. SSL/Hostname Verification Bypass

**Candidate scale**: N sites / N modules

#### C3-s1 — {{Description}}
- [ ] **`{{Path}}`**
  - Checks:
    - [ ] `HostnameVerifier` returns true unconditionally?
    - [ ] `X509TrustManager.checkServerTrusted` is empty?
    - [ ] `ALLOW_ALL_HOSTNAME_VERIFIER` constant used?
    - [ ] Applied to production HTTPS connections (not test-only)?
  - Verdict:
    - [ ] Vulnerable
    - [ ] Not vulnerable (test-only)

---

## C4. Sensitive Data Logging

**Candidate scale**: N matches / N modules

#### C4-s1 — {{Description}}
- [ ] **`{{Path}}`**
  - Checks:
    - [ ] PII/credential fields logged without masking?
    - [ ] Full request/response object logged?
    - [ ] Authorization header logged in plain text?
    - [ ] Log output accessible to unauthorized parties?
  - Verdict:
    - [ ] Vulnerable
    - [ ] Not vulnerable (masked)

---

## C5. Unsafe Deserialization (XML/XStream/XXE)

**Candidate scale**: N sites / N modules

#### C5-s1 — {{Description}}
- [ ] **`{{Path}}`**
  - Checks:
    - [ ] `XStream` instantiated without `setupDefaultSecurity`?
    - [ ] `allowTypes`/`allowTypesByWildcard` absent?
    - [ ] `DocumentBuilderFactory` without disallow-doctype-decl?
    - [ ] Reachable from external input without auth? (C1 x C5 chain?)
  - Verdict:
    - [ ] Vulnerable
    - [ ] Not vulnerable (hardened)
    - [ ] **Critical** (C1 x C5 cross-cluster chain)

